.TH LYFY 1 "2026-10-28" "lyfy" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lyfy \- declarative system maintenance for Arch Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lyfy
.RI [ options ]
.B lint
.br
.B lyfy
.RI [ options ]
.B save
.br
.B lyfy
.RI [ options ]
.B apply
.RB [ \-\-write ]
.br
.B lyfy
.RI [ options ]
.B fmt
.RB [ \-\-write ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lyfy
inspects an Arch Linux system, records concrete host configuration and plans
reconciliation with saved state.
The supported release architecture is x86_64.
.PP
There are exactly four commands:
.BR lint ,
.BR fmt ,
.BR save
and
.BR apply .
Global options may appear before or after the command.
Each setting has a snake_case option and a corresponding
.B LYFY_UPPER_CASE
environment variable.
Precedence is option, environment, TOML configuration, then default.
See
.BR lyfy.conf (5)
for settings, scope defaults and configuration lookup.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B lint
Inspect the Arch policy without changing the managed system.
Checks include pending pacnew/pacsave files, pacman database consistency,
missing package files, package metadata drift, files without a package owner,
orphan dependencies, running kernel state, the configured UKI policy and
failed systemd units.
Incomplete and skipped checks are reported explicitly.
.IP
UKI is a lyfy policy, not an Arch Linux requirement.
Unowned files, orphan packages and modified package metadata require review.
.TP
.B save
Capture files, normal Unix permissions, ownership, symlinks and optional
package inventory for the selected host.
Files edited in place are saved directly, without templates.
.IP
Git is the default storage format.
The repository contains ordinary payload files and JSON metadata under
.IR hosts/host/ .
Saving commits the host state locally on the current attached branch and
creates no empty commit for unchanged state.
Existing repository changes must be committed, stashed or resolved first.
Saving never implicitly pushes or merges.
.IP
.B \-\-base_host
selects an optional common base when saving.
The resulting host overlay pins that base to an immutable revision.
Saving common later does not rewrite already saved host overlays.
.TP
.B apply
Plan reconciliation with the selected host and snapshot.
The plan compares desired content, live content and the last applied receipt
for the same host, root and home directory.
A different existing target on first deployment is a conflict.
.IP
.B \-\-write
executes a conflict-free plan, backing up file preimages and recording a
private transaction journal before target writes.
.B \-\-overwrite true
permits reviewed conflicting replacements.
Tracked deletions additionally require
.BR "\-\-prune true" .
Untracked files are retained, and directory deletion is nonrecursive.
.IP
Package restoration additionally requires
.BR "\-\-install_packages true" ,
existing root privileges and text display.
It uses a full pacman upgrade for missing native packages and restores
affected installation reasons.
Missing foreign packages require deliberate handling.
Extra packages are not removed and recorded versions are not forced.
.TP
.B fmt
Plan supported deterministic policy fixes.
.B \-\-write
executes them through the same backup and journal mechanism as apply.
Currently only pacnew files identical to their active configuration are
removed automatically.
Other findings require manual review.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config_file " path"
Use this required TOML file instead of XDG configuration lookup.
The environment equivalent is
.BR LYFY_CONFIG_FILE .
This selector cannot be specified inside the configuration file itself.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " text|json"
Select result display.
Interactive package execution requires text display.
.TP
.B \-\-write
Grant execution permission for apply or fmt.
This permission has no configuration key or environment equivalent.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Show the executable version.
.PP
All configuration settings documented in
.BR lyfy.conf (5)
also accept the corresponding
.B \-\-snake_case
global option.
Booleans require an explicit true or false value.
Comma-separated list overrides replace the lower-priority list.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
lyfy lint
lyfy save \-\-host common
lyfy save \-\-host laptop \-\-base_host common
lyfy apply \-\-host laptop
lyfy apply \-\-host laptop \-\-write
lyfy fmt
.fi
.PP
Review the plan before selecting overwrite, prune or package restoration.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lyfy/config.toml
User configuration, defaulting to
.IR ~/.config/lyfy/config.toml .
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/lyfy/config.toml
System configuration locations searched after the user's file.
The default directory is
.IR /etc/xdg .
The first readable configuration file wins as a whole.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/lyfy
Default state repository, falling back to
.IR ~/.local/share/lyfy .
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/lyfy
Receipts, locks and transaction journals, falling back to
.IR ~/.local/state/lyfy .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested operation succeeded.
An apply preview with planned changes and no conflicts succeeds.
.TP
.B 1
Findings, conflicts or pending fmt fixes remain.
.TP
.B 2
An operational or configuration error prevented completion.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Individual file replacements are atomic; a multi-file operation is not one
atomic filesystem transaction.
Failures leave original file objects and a recovery journal in
.IR state_dir/transactions/ .
Automatic rollback, crash resume, AUR builds and boot migration are not
implemented.
.PP
Capture rejects hardlinks, regular-file/directory extended attributes,
special permission bits, special files and non-UTF-8 names.
Symbolic links are recorded without following their targets.
Target writes refuse symlink parents.
Stop concurrent edits and package transactions while capturing or applying
state; lyfy does not freeze the filesystem.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lyfy.conf (5),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR bootctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR git (1)
